{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you back to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, thanks for seeing me. I was just discharged three days ago, but yesterday the pain around my G-tube got a lot worse. It’s different—more focused there, not all over like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Was there any injury? Did you lift something or fall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I was just walking around. No heavy lifting or falls. I thought maybe taking a night off from tube feeds would help, but it didn’t."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fever, nausea, or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. I’ve been keeping down clear liquids—Ensure and Carnation breakfast drink. Last bowel movement was yesterday, normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Let me examine you quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your G-tube looks okay—no redness or signs of infection. But I notice tenderness right around the site, especially when you tense your abdomen. That’s called Carnett’s sign, which suggests the pain might be from the abdominal wall muscles, not inside the belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so it’s not the tube itself or an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. We also did an X-ray called a KUB. It shows no blockage or free air, which is reassuring. But there is some gaseous distention in the stomach area, possibly from your prior gastric bypass anatomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could that be making the pain worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but the main focus now seems to be the abdominal wall. We’ll hold your tube feeds overnight to rest your gut and restart them tomorrow if you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ve been using the oxycodone, but it didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. We’re going to adjust your pain meds. We’ll increase your gabapentin from 300 mg to 600 mg three times a day. It works better for nerve or musculoskeletal pain like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on that before. Should help. What about the erythromycin and rifaximin I started last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue both. They’re for bacterial overgrowth, which you’ve had before. We’ll finish a 14-day course to make sure it’s under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I’ve been worried this pain means something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But right now, everything looks stable. No signs of infection or obstruction. We’ll keep monitoring you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been feeling anxious about it all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-08-31 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve arranged for you to meet with a social worker today. They can help with coping strategies and connect you with your outpatient therapist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-08-31 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain now? Any change since we adjusted the meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-08-31 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but maybe a little less sharp. I’m not in distress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-08-31 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good progress. We’ll keep an eye on it overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We checked your labs this morning. Your white blood cell count is a bit low—2.8—but it’s improved from yesterday and not due to infection. We’ll repeat it in a week as a precaution."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this level, especially since you’re not sick. It’s slightly below your baseline, but no medication or infection seems to be causing it. Just a quick check in a week to make sure it stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to restart your tube feeds at the goal rate—50 mL/hr of Jevity 1.5. Nutrition recommends this formula for better tolerance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using Jevity 1.2. Is the change okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-09-01 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s safe. But you’ll need your outpatient provider to prescribe it. Let your GI doctor know when you follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-09-01 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain been since restarting feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-09-01 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No worse. Actually, feels about like my usual baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-09-01 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. And your G-tube site? Any redness or warmth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-09-01 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a little redness, but it’s not getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-09-01 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nurse noted minimal erythema, but it’s improving. We’ll keep the mupirocin ointment on it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-09-01 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if things stay on track. Pain is at baseline, you’re tolerating feeds, and labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-09-01 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Should I call my GI doctor soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-09-01 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, definitely. Continue working with them on your chronic pain. We’ve updated your meds—higher gabapentin, same antidepressants and acid reducers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-09-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Your pain is stable, you’re moving well, and labs are okay. Remember: finish the erythromycin and rifaximin, keep the CBC follow-up, and talk to your GI doctor about any new concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-09-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better knowing it’s not something dangerous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-09-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and keep in touch with your team."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-08-31 16:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-09-02 15:02:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with acute-on-chronic abdominal pain localized near her gastrostomy tube site, three days after a prior discharge. The pain was focal and tender on examination with a positive Carnett’s sign, suggesting abdominal wall musculature as the source. Imaging showed a nonobstructive bowel gas pattern and gaseous distention of the stomach, likely related to her complex surgical history, but no evidence of infection or free air. Tube feeds were held overnight and successfully restarted. Gabapentin was increased to 600 mg TID for improved pain control, and she continued erythromycin and rifaximin for bacterial overgrowth. Mild leukopenia improved without intervention. She met with a social worker, discussed coping strategies, and was discharged home with stable pain, a plan to follow up with her GI doctor, and instructions to repeat CBC in one week.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Decreased white blood cell count, unspecified",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Acute gastritis without bleeding"
    ]
  }
}
